queued behind it on the shared\\\\n        # stream is then pinned to the attention frontier → the depth-2\\\\n        # frozen-weight prefetch collapses to ~depth-1 (= the documented\\\\n        # ~48 ms/step all-frozen-split stall).  Same failure as the abandoned\\\\n        # _h2d_serial gate.  The old \\\\\\\"+95 ms\\\\\\\" warning was real.\\\\n        #\\\\n        # The real fix (TODO) is to BREAK the load↔unload↔attention coupling so\\\\n        # the KV load no longer waits attention: e.g. copy the new-token tail\\\\n        # aside to a small staging buffer right after reshape_and_cache (early in\\\\n        # the layer), unload D2H from that staging asynchronously, and let\\\\n        # load(L+1) wait only that early tiny D2D — then aliasing is execution-\\\\n        # neutral and this can default ON.  Until then, opt-in for measurement.\\\\n        if (os.getenv(\\\\\\\"TIERED_SERVE_RAW_KV_ALIAS\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"\\\\n                and not DualMemoryLoader.use_kv_comp\\\\n                and os.getenv(\\\\\\\"TIERED_SERVE_KV_H2D_ON_WEIGHT\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"\\\\n                and os.getenv(\\\\\\\"TIERED_SERVE_KV_DOUBLE_BUFFER\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"\\\\n                and self.n_layers % 2 == 0):\\\\n            self.load_kv_stream = self.load_weight_stream\\\\n            logger.info(\\\\n                \\\\\\\"[kv-decode] RAW KV H2D aliased onto load_weight_stream \\\\\\\"\\\\n                \\\\\\\"(opt-in; clean bracket but +25-31%% TPOT until tail-staging \\\\\\\"\\\\n                \\\\\\\"decouple lands)\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n        # Single timing flag: TIERED_SERVE_COLLECT_TIME enables both per-step\\\\n        # CUDA-event collection AND the aggregated Exec/Load/Stall breakdown\\\\n        # summary in calc_times() (they were two separate vars; unified).\\\\n        self.collect_times = (os.getenv(\\\\\\\"TIERED_SERVE_COLLECT_TIME\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\